Formatting Principles for Visual Alignment
​Numbers (Right-Aligned): Right-aligning digits ensures decimal points align vertically, allowing quick visual comparison of magnitudes (as seen in standard financial ledgers).  
​Labels (Left-Aligned): Left-aligning text aligns the starting letters, following natural scanning patterns for text.  
​4. Key Takeaways & Standards
​Core String Methods: Master strip, split, join, and replace.  
​Format Spec Order: Always specify alignment, width, and decimals in that order.  
​Report Layout Rule:
​Align labels left.  
​Align numbers right.  
​Ensure decimal points line up vertically.  
​Readability Test: A report is properly formatted if you can read the values cleanly without shif
